shape theory {
  type: axiom
  layer: 0
  """
// The formal derivation of persistence structure.
// Everything here derives from one definition: persistence is the
// capacity to change while maintaining continuity (Def 2.1).
//
// This namespace IS the derivation. Each shape is a definition,
// theorem, or law. Deps track what each result derives from.
// The derivation graph is the theory.
//
// Namespace:
//   theory.axiom         - The persistence definition (Def 2.1)
//   theory.shape         - Shape as primitive (Def 2.2)
//   theory.structure     - Structure S (Def 3.1)
//   theory.character     - Character C (Def 3.2)
//   theory.moment        - Moment M (Def 3.3)
//   theory.transformation - Transformation law M'=f(C,S)
//   theory.minimal       - The minimal shape
//   theory.contact       - Contact and its forms
//   theory.coherence     - Coherence and the four laws
//   theory.emergence     - Emergent composition
//   theory.fractal       - Fractal coherence
//   theory.dimension     - Dimensionality and chirality
//   theory.mixing        - Self-transformation and mixing angles
//   theory.coupling      - Coupled shape systems
//   theory.forcing       - Forcing, collapse, resolution
//   theory.branching     - Branching, distribution, canopy
//   theory.constants     - Structural constants
//   theory.operations    - Structural operations
//   theory.landscape     - Instantiation and the landscape
//   theory.algebra       - The algebra of shapes
//   theory.category      - Shape category theory
//   theory.sets          - Shape set theory
//   theory.completeness  - Persistence completeness
  """
}
